---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { business } from '../config/business';
const sections = [
  { id: 'responsibility', label: 'Who is responsible' },
  { id: 'information', label: 'Information collected' },
  { id: 'purpose', label: 'How information is used' },
  { id: 'providers', label: 'Storage and providers' },
  { id: 'retention', label: 'Retention' },
  { id: 'rights', label: 'Your rights' },
  { id: 'cookies', label: 'Cookies and changes' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How Presence Web Services handles information shared through an enquiry, and the choices you have about your personal information."
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="responsibility">
    <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
    {!business.launchReady && (
      <p class="service-note">
        Private test policy. The controller’s complete legal identity, correspondence address,
        retention schedule and provider arrangements are awaiting confirmation before public launch.
      </p>
    )}
    <p>
      Presence Web Services uses enquiry information to respond to people asking about its website
      and online presence services. This policy covers enquiries through this website, rather than
      the processing arrangements for a paid client project.
    </p>
    {business.legalName && (
      <p>
        The data controller is {business.legalName}
        {business.correspondenceAddress && `, ${business.correspondenceAddress}`}.
      </p>
    )}
    <p>
      For privacy questions, use the{' '}
      <a class="inline-link" href="/contact/">
        contact form
      </a>
      {business.email && (
        <>
          {' '}
          or email{' '}
          <a class="inline-link" href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>
            {business.email}
          </a>
        </>
      )}
      . Explain that your message concerns personal information. Do not include identity documents,
      passwords or sensitive information in the form.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="information">
    <h2>2. Information collected</h2>
    <p>
      The enquiry form asks for your contact name, business name, email address and main goal or
      concern. You may also choose to provide a website address, Google Business Profile or Maps
      link, location, service preference and telephone number.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you request a review, Presence may look at publicly available business information that you
      identify, such as your website and Google profile. Correspondence and notes relevant to your
      enquiry may be kept with your submission.
    </p>
    <p>
      The hosting infrastructure may process IP addresses and request details. The application uses
      a keyed hash of the request IP for short-lived rate limits and does not store the raw IP with
      enquiries. Please only share personal information you are entitled to provide.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="purpose">
    <h2>3. How and why information is used</h2>
    <p>
      Information is used to respond to your message, carry out a requested public audit, discuss
      suitable support and prepare a proposal if you want one. It is also used where necessary to
      keep the service secure or meet a legal obligation.
    </p>
    <p>
      Where you enquire on your own behalf about a possible contract, the lawful basis is taking
      steps at your request before entering a contract. For business enquiries made on behalf of an
      organisation, and for appropriate record keeping and security, Presence relies on legitimate
      interests in responding to relevant enquiries and running a safe service, balanced against
      your rights. Legal obligations apply where records must be retained by law.
    </p>
    <p>
      Sending an enquiry does not sign you up to marketing. Presence does not sell enquiry
      information or use it to make automated decisions with legal or similarly significant effects.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="providers">
    <h2>4. Storage, service providers and transfers</h2>
    <p>
      The private test website runs on OpenAI Sites using Cloudflare hosting and a Cloudflare D1
      database. Valid enquiry details are saved in that database. Only authorised owner access can
      retrieve or delete them. A successful save does not send an email notification.
    </p>
    <p>
      Email sent directly to contact@presencewebservices.co.uk is forwarded by Cloudflare Email
      Routing to the owner's Gmail inbox. This is separate from the website form. OpenAI, Cloudflare
      and Google process information under their own applicable service terms. Their contractual
      roles, processing locations, subprocessors and international transfer safeguards must be
      confirmed before the public service starts. No UK-only storage claim is made.
    </p>
    <p>
      Presence limits access to information to what is needed for the enquiry or agreed work. No
      enquiry information is published on this website, and the form does not store your details in
      browser storage.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="retention">
    <h2>5. Keeping and deleting information</h2>
    <p>
      Private test enquiries have a one-day expiry. Expired rows are deleted on the next submission,
      owner API review or explicit owner purge. Without activity, records may remain stored until
      that purge runs. This does not guarantee deletion at the exact expiry time. Only dummy details
      should be used during this test.
    </p>
    {business.privacyRetention && <p>{business.privacyRetention}</p>}
    <p>
      The production enquiry retention period is awaiting owner approval; public launch is blocked
      until it is configured and published. When information is no longer needed, it should be
      deleted from the database and any related correspondence, subject to provider backup cycles
      and legal obligations. If you become a client, a separate agreement may explain the records
      needed for the paid service.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="rights">
    <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on the circumstances, you may request access to your personal information,
      correction of inaccurate information, erasure, restriction or portability. You may object to
      processing based on legitimate interests. These rights have legal limits and may not apply to
      every record.
    </p>
    <p>
      Use the{' '}
      <a class="inline-link" href="/contact/">
        contact form
      </a>{' '}
      to make a request, with enough information to locate your enquiry. Proportionate identity
      verification may be needed before information is disclosed. A request will be handled within
      the applicable statutory time limit.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can also complain to the UK Information Commissioner’s Office. Visit{' '}
      <a class="inline-link" href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="external">
        ico.org.uk
      </a>{' '}
      for information about raising a data protection concern.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="cookies">
    <h2>7. Cookies and policy changes</h2>
    <p>
      This website does not include advertising trackers or analytics scripts. After a saved
      enquiry, an essential, signed receipt cookie lasts ten minutes so the confirmation page can
      show a genuine receipt. It contains an opaque record identifier, expiry and signature, not the
      enquiry details. It is HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax and Secure over HTTPS. The private hosting
      sign-in service may set its own authentication cookies. Hosting infrastructure may use
      technical measures needed to deliver and secure the service. If optional analytics or other
      tracking is introduced, this policy and any required consent controls must be updated first.
    </p>
    <p>
      The policy should be reviewed when the website, enquiry process or service providers change.
      The version available on this page describes the current website implementation.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
